From 0b5ea7fa4456353df5f267235a7f0755edc5b3d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:58:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep runner startup sweeps out of fresh test
 attempts

Why: the host-slot deleted-tree test observed SIGTERM (-15), not its expected SIGKILL. A concurrent nested runner scans the shared test scratch root; generic pruning reaps deleted cwd processes even when no entry is old. The deliberately deleted fixture cwd was mistaken for an abandoned process.

Scope runner cleanup to selected idle entries while retaining generic deleted-cwd reclamation by default. Recheck the selected entries after owned-process rescue. Preserve the original slot test and retry policy unchanged.

Proof: owned-child replay fails on base with -15; 124 tests pass with retries disabled across seven consumer files, including real holder SIGSTOP/SIGCONT duty cycles. Both dispatch and post-rescue-filter mutants are killed. scripts/check --base origin/main passes.
